==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Cat Projector''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Catophone''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Cat Toaster on surface seems to have good use, but much like [[Delinquent Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Delinquent Cat]], his main issue is his very long cooldown. Unlike [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], whose application expands wildly with his high stats and disposability, Cat Toaster doesn't even offer serviceable stats. Furthermore, his anti-Angel abilities are outclassed in various ways, as most Angels have low range and the exceptions often have much better counters like talented [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]], not to mention his poor uptime and [[Juliet Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Juliet Cat]]'s Freeze. There's no point in using it at all.

==='''True Form'''===
Catophone gains more stats and [[Barrier Breaker]], as well as increased [[Slow|Slow]] duration. Unfortunately, none of these improve it meaningfully. Its stats are still too low to be usable, and same goes for its 5-second Slow due to its activation chance remaining at 30%. Barrier Breaker, while seemingly useful, is hindered by other circumstances. Most Barriers won't stand a beating, but even if they could, the Breakerblast Cannon, [[Fencer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fencer Cat]], [[Li'l Gross Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Macho Legs Cat]] and [[Space Cat (Rare Cat)|Space Marine Cat]] could all do the job better, with Fencer getting it in every time. This leaves the unit at an extremely awkward position where all its niches are covered by far superior alternatives when it can't even get the job done.

However, there's still an use for this unit: being an Area Attacking Barrier Breaker. If you cannot stack Fencer Cat to deal with a group of [[UltraBaaBaa]]s, Catophone proves to be decently useful against them, but since the Barrier Breaker is not guaranteed, Catophone's Area Attack Barrier Breaker use is situational at best.

==='''Talents'''===
The first talent is Barrier Breaker, making this unit more consistent at shattering barriers, though the chance is still not guaranteed, going from 20% to 40% when maxed out. Target Alien allows Catophone to get some extra mileage from Barrier Breaker by slowing the Aliens it would hit, but [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] already exists for this purpose and has better overall stats and crowd-control capability. The Health and Attack buffs are not worth investing into as Catophone's stats are poor. Cost Down puts less of a strain on your wallet and allows Catophone to be stacked better, otherwise use other Crowd-Controllers with better consistency. Because of the aforementioned issues, Catophone is ultimately not worth any NP investment.

==='''Orb'''===
Due to being outclassed, Catophone isn't worth using a Talent Orb for. Defense Up vs Angels or Defense Up vs Aliens are its best option nonetheless.

